ative  timing schedule if not our colleagues of  DG come have this document ready for you  in the always latest version please do  understand that these are all timings  that are necessarily indicative our work  depends on the availability and on the  robustness of the data that we are  receiving from the Member States be it  exit polls estimations or later on  results so for the concrete timing  tonight at around 1815 so there is  already a small delay of about 10  minutes our contractor cantar will  provide national estimates for the first  seven countries Austria Cyprus Germany  Greece Ireland Malta and the Netherlands  we will update with further exit polls  at 7:00 and at 8:00 by five more  countries which brings us then to 8:15  2050 in Brussels time when we are  planning to release a first EP  aggregation based on the exit polls and  estimates from these twelve member  states and pre-electoral voting  intention survey data for 16 member  states  so this first aggregation and that's  important is not based on any election  result yet and therefore due to the  available information at that point in  time it will also further evolve  throughout the evening with an update  expected for Aston line and after 10  o'clock this evening after the close of  all polling stations in the U at 11  o'clock tonight member states will then  start publishing their official results  of the European elections and we can  plan to release our first result  projection for the European elections  2019 based on official results from 22  members  dates at 11:15 tonight updates will then  come in at the hour and we expect to  publish the last update for this night  around 2:30 in the morning which will  allow us to have more or less a robust  picture from the UK no further updates  are then planned for the rest of the  night giving you a small risk in the  night we expect releasing further  updates than in the morning around 10:00  a.m. now for the issue of turnout as  jean has already 